hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"301","**\nNarrated to us Muḥammad ibn Bashshār (Bundār), narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar and Ibn Abī ʿAdiyy, from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah, from Qatādah, from Anas ibn Mālik, from Mālik ibn Ṣaʿṣaʿah (RA), a man from his people, that the Prophet of Allāh ﷺ said:\n\n*\While I was at the House (the Kaʿbah)"," in a state between sleep and wakefulness"," I heard a voice saying: 'Take between the three","' so I was brought a golden basin containing water from Zamzam. He (the narrator) said: 'My chest was opened to such-and-such","' Qatādah said: 'I asked what he meant by that","' and he said: 'To the lower part of his belly.' Then my heart was extracted"," washed with the water of Zamzam"," and then returned to its place. It was then filled with faith and wisdom. Then I was brought a white beast"," called al-Burāq"," larger than a donkey and smaller than a mule"," whose stride reached the farthest point of its sight. I was mounted upon it"," and then we set off until we reached the lowest heaven.\n\nJibrīl (AS) sought permission to enter"," and it was said: 'Who is this?' He said: 'Jibrīl.' It was said: 'And who is with you?' He said: 'Muḥammad.' It was said: 'And has he been sent for?' He said: 'Yes.' So the gate was opened for us. He (the gatekeeper) said: 'Welcome! What an excellent arrival this is.'\n\nI passed by Ādam (AS)"," so I said: 'O Jibrīl"," who is this?' He said: 'This is your father Ādam.' So I greeted him"," and he said: 'Welcome"," O righteous son and righteous Prophet.'\n\nThen we proceeded until we reached the second heaven. Jibrīl sought permission"," and it was said: 'Who is this?' He said: 'Jibrīl.' It was said: 'And who is with you?' He said: 'Muḥammad.' It was said: 'And has he been sent for?' He said: 'Yes.' So the gate was opened for us. He said: 'Welcome! What an excellent arrival this is.'\n\nI passed by Yaḥyā and ʿĪsā (AS)"," so I said: 'O Jibrīl"," who are these two?' He said: 'Yaḥyā and ʿĪsā.' Saʿīd said: 'I think he said in his narration: \""The two maternal cousins.\""' So I greeted them"," and they said: 'Welcome"," O righteous brother and righteous Prophet.'\n\nThen we proceeded until we reached the third heaven. Jibrīl sought permission"," and it was said: 'Who is this?' He said: 'Jibrīl.' It was said: 'And who is with you?' He said: 'Muḥammad.' It was said: 'And has he been sent for?' He said: 'Yes.' So the gate was opened for us"," and he said: 'Welcome! What an excellent arrival this is.'\n\nI passed by Yūsuf (AS)"," so I greeted him"," and he said: 'Welcome"," O righteous Prophet and righteous brother.'\n\nThen we proceeded to the fourth heaven"," and the conversation was similar to that of Jibrīl and them. I passed by Idrīs (AS)"," so I greeted him"," and he said: 'Welcome"," O righteous brother and righteous Prophet.'\n\nThen we reached the fifth heaven"," and I passed by Hārūn (AS)"," so I greeted him"," and he said: 'Welcome"," O righteous brother and righteous Prophet.'\n\nThen we proceeded to the sixth heaven"," and I passed by Mūsā (AS)"," so I greeted him"," and he said: 'Welcome"," O righteous brother and righteous Prophet.' When I passed him"," he wept. Then I returned to the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary (Sidrah al-Muntahā).\n\nThe Prophet of Allāh ﷺ informed that its fruits are like the water-skins of Hajar"," and its leaves are like the ears of elephants. He also informed that he saw four rivers flowing from its base: two visible rivers and two hidden rivers. I said: 'O Jibrīl"," what are these rivers?' He said: 'As for the two hidden rivers"," they are in Paradise. As for the two visible ones"," they are the Nile and the Euphrates.'\n\nThen the Bayt al-Maʿmūr (the Frequented House) was raised for us. I said: 'O Jibrīl"," what is this?' He said: 'This is the Bayt al-Maʿmūr. Every day"," seventy thousand angels enter it. When they leave"," they never return to it again.'\n\nThen I was brought two vessels: one of wine and the other of milk. They were presented to me"," and I chose the milk. It was said: 'You have chosen correctly. Allāh will guide your nation to the natural disposition (fitrah).' Then fifty prayers were prescribed for me every day. I set off with them until I reached Mūsā (AS)"," who said: 'What have you been commanded with?' I said: 'Fifty prayers every day.' He said: 'Your nation cannot bear that. I have tested the Children of Isrāʾīl before you"," and I have dealt with them most severely. Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten it for your nation.'\n\nSo I returned"," and He lightened it by five. I continued to go back and forth between my Lord and Mūsā (AS)"," each time reducing it further"," until I returned with five prayers every day. He (Mūsā) said: 'Your nation cannot bear that. I have tested the people before you and dealt with the Children of Isrāʾīl most severely. Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten it for your nation.'\n\nHe (the Prophet ﷺ) said: 'I kept beseeching my Lord until I felt shy"," but I was content and submitted. Then it was announced: \""I have confirmed My obligation"," lightened it for My servants"," and made every good deed tenfold.\""'\""*"""
"302","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar al-Bundar, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Ibn Abi 'Adiyy, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Malik ibn Sa'sa'ah (RA), a man from his people, that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\While I was at the House (the Ka'bah)"," between sleeping and waking"," I heard a speaker saying: 'Take the middle of the three.' So I was brought a golden basin containing water from Zamzam. Then my chest was opened from here to here\"" — Qatadah said: \""I asked what he meant by 'here to here","' and he said: 'From the collarbone to the lower part of the abdomen.'\""\n\nThen my heart was extracted"," washed with the water of Zamzam"," then returned to its place"," and filled with faith and wisdom. Then I was brought a white animal"," called al-Buraq"," larger than a donkey but smaller than a mule"," whose stride reached the farthest point of its sight. I mounted it"," and then we set off until we reached the lowest heaven.\n\nJibril (AS) sought permission to enter"," and it was said: 'Who is this?' He replied: 'Jibril.' It was said: 'And who is with you?' He said: 'Muhammad (ﷺ).' It was said: 'Has he been sent for?' He replied: 'Yes.' So the gate was opened for us. It was said: 'Welcome! What an excellent arrival this is.'\n\nI passed by Adam (AS)"," so I said: 'O Jibril"," who is this?' He said: 'This is your father Adam.' So I greeted him"," and he said: 'Welcome"," O righteous son and righteous Prophet.'\n\nThen we proceeded until we reached the second heaven. Jibril sought permission"," and it was said: 'Who is this?' He replied: 'Jibril.' It was said: 'And who is with you?' He said: 'Muhammad (ﷺ).' It was said: 'Has he been sent for?' He replied: 'Yes.' So the gate was opened for us. It was said: 'Welcome! What an excellent arrival this is.'\n\nI passed by Yahya (AS) and 'Isa (AS)"," so I said: 'O Jibril"," who are these?' He said: 'Yahya and 'Isa.' Sa'id said: \""I think he said in his narration: 'The two maternal cousins.'\""\n\nSo I greeted them"," and they said: 'Welcome"," O righteous brother and righteous Prophet.'\n\nThen we proceeded until we reached the third heaven. Jibril sought permission"," and it was said: 'Who is this?' He replied: 'Jibril.' It was said: 'And who is with you?' He said: 'Muhammad (ﷺ).' It was said: 'Has he been sent for?' He replied: 'Yes.' So the gate was opened for us"," and it was said: 'Welcome! What an excellent arrival this is.'\n\nI passed by Yusuf (AS)"," so I greeted him"," and he said: 'Welcome"," O righteous Prophet and righteous brother.'\n\nThen we proceeded to the fourth heaven"," and the conversation was similar to what Jibril and they had said. I passed by Idris (AS)"," so I greeted him"," and he said: 'Welcome"," O righteous brother and righteous Prophet.'\n\nThen we reached the fifth heaven"," and I passed by Harun (AS)"," so I greeted him"," and he said: 'Welcome"," O righteous brother and righteous Prophet.'\n\nThen we proceeded to the sixth heaven"," and I passed by Musa (AS)"," so I greeted him"," and he said: 'Welcome"," O righteous brother and righteous Prophet.' When I passed him"," he wept. Then I reached the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary (Sidrat al-Muntaha).\n\nThe Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) informed that its fruits were like the jars of Hajar"," and its leaves were like the ears of elephants. He also informed that he saw four rivers flowing from its base: two hidden and two manifest. I said: 'O Jibril"," what are these rivers?' He said: 'As for the two hidden rivers"," they are in Paradise. As for the two manifest rivers"," they are the Nile and the Euphrates.'\n\nThen the Bayt al-Ma'mur (the Frequented House) was raised for us. I said: 'O Jibril"," what is this?' He said: 'This is the Bayt al-Ma'mur. Every day"," seventy thousand angels enter it"," and when they leave"," they never return to it again.'\n\nThen I was brought two vessels: one containing wine and the other milk. They were presented to me"," and I chose the milk. It was said: 'You have chosen correctly. Allah will guide your nation to the natural disposition (fitrah).'\n\nThen fifty prayers were prescribed for me every day. I returned with them until I reached Musa (AS)"," who said: 'What have you been commanded?' I replied: 'Fifty prayers every day.' He said: 'Your nation cannot bear that. I have tested the Children of Israel before you"," and I have dealt with them more severely. Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten the burden for your nation.'\n\nSo I returned to my Lord"," and He made it fifty to ten. Then I kept going back and forth between my Lord and Musa (AS)"," until He made it five prayers. Musa (AS) still said: 'Your nation cannot bear that. I have tested the people before you and dealt with the Children of Israel more severely. Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten the burden for your nation.'\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'I kept asking until I felt shy"," but I was content and submitted. Then a call was made: \""I have fulfilled My obligation"," and I have lightened it for My servants. I have made every good deed worth ten like it.\""'\n\n---"""
